{% doc %}
  Page title, description, canonical address and link-preview tags, from Shopify's Skeleton theme.

  - The tab title uses the site's words for the cart, search and 404 pages, joins its parts with
    commas and one bar before the name, and names it once (DESIGN.md §0: no dashes). The name is
    the programme the header logo shows: Gordon Smith Gallery, Artists for Kids or The Gordon and
    Marion Smith Foundation (DS-121). Checkout and emails keep the store name.
  - A page shares its own picture as the link preview: a page's hero image, an exhibition's key
    image, a work's first image, an artist's portrait, a lesson's cover. Else the store's.
  - A frame's page (product type Frame) asks search engines not to list it (DS-137).
  - Without a description of its own, an entry describes itself: a work by its label, an artist
    by name, nationality, dates and the start of the biography, a grouping by its introduction, a
    page by its intro or the start of its text. An artist without a biography and a grouping
    without an introduction say how many works the collection holds. An exhibition's description
    starts with its dates. A page with nothing to say prints no description, and only the home
    page uses the store's (DS-155).
  - A written description comes first: a page's in its Release description field until release
    (custom.release_description, as DS-39 stages a page's text), the home page's in Theme
    settings. Shopify makes a description from a page's or a product's text when the store has
    none, and drops the spaces between its lines ("AvenueNorth Vancouver"). A description that
    starts as the text does is that one, so the page's own words are used instead, and an
    edition describes itself by its label, medium, edition and size (DS-160).
  - A work's and an edition's title is its label in plain letters, "Artist, Title, year", from
    the entry's or the product's fields, never the product title, whose italics are Unicode
    letters a search engine can't read (DS-156).
  - The link preview names the programme, as the title does, and says what its picture shows and
    how large it is (DS-155).
  - A grouping's works page by 24, under an address Shopify names itself
    (?page_b81ab1c2=2), which its canonical address and current_page leave out. So page 2 would
    name page 1 as its canonical address and carry its title. The same paginate tag here, which
    reads nothing, gives the page's number and address: each page names itself, says "page 2"
    in its title, and names the pages before and after it (DS-168).
  - Search engines may show the page's picture large and quote as much of its text as they
    need (max-image-preview, max-snippet, max-video-preview), so a work's picture isn't cut to
    a thumbnail in results and AI answers (DS-169).
  - Structured data for search and answer engines comes from gs-data (DS-154), an edition's
    too, in place of Shopify's structured_data filter (DS-159).

  @example
  {% render 'meta-tags' %}
{% enddoc %}
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta http-equiv="X-UA-Compatible" content="IE=edge">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">

{%- liquid
  assign og_title = page_title | default: shop.name
  assign og_url = canonical_url | default: request.origin
  assign og_type = 'website'

  # The entry's own picture and words, used when the page has none of its own.
  assign own_image = nil
  assign entry_text = ''
  assign entry_label = ''
  assign lead_in = ''
  assign works_note = ''
  if request.page_type == 'page'
    assign own_image = page.metafields.custom.hero_image.value
    assign written = page.metafields.custom.release_description.value
    assign made_from = page.content
    assign entry_text = page.metafields.custom.intro.value
    if entry_text == blank
      # The start of the page's text, as gs-page-text picks it (DS-39). A space before each tag
      # keeps the words of two paragraphs apart.
      assign body = page.content
      if page.metafields.custom.release_body != blank
        assign body = page.metafields.custom.release_body.value
      endif
      assign entry_text = body | replace: '<', ' <' | strip_html | strip_newlines | split: ' ' | join: ' ' | replace: ' ,', ',' | replace: ' .', '.' | truncatewords: 30
    endif
  elsif request.page_type == 'product'
    assign f = product.metafields.custom
    assign made_from = product.description
    if f.artist.value != blank and f.artwork_title.value != blank
      assign entry_label = f.artist.value | append: ', ' | append: f.artwork_title.value
      if f.year.value != blank
        assign entry_label = entry_label | append: ', ' | append: f.year.value
      endif
      # The label's facts, in the order of the page (DS-16): medium, edition, size.
      assign entry_text = entry_label
      assign facts = 'medium,edition,dimensions' | split: ','
      for fact in facts
        assign value = f[fact].value | strip
        if value != blank
          # Each fact starts with a capital. Not capitalize, which lower-cases the rest.
          assign first_char = value | slice: 0 | upcase
          assign rest = value | slice: 1, value.size
          assign entry_text = entry_text | append: '. ' | append: first_char | append: rest
        endif
      endfor
      assign entry_text = entry_text | truncate: 300
    endif
  elsif metaobject != blank
    case metaobject.system.type
      when 'exhibition'
        assign own_image = metaobject.key_image.value
        if metaobject.start_date.value != blank
          capture lead_in
            render 'gs-date-range', start: metaobject.start_date.value, end: metaobject.end_date.value
          endcapture
          # The dates' no-break spaces (U+00A0) are for the page, not for a description.
          assign nb = ' '
          assign lead_in = lead_in | strip | replace: nb, ' ' | append: '. '
        endif
        assign entry_text = metaobject.summary.value | newline_to_br | strip_newlines | replace: '<br />', ' '
      when 'artwork'
        for image in metaobject.images.value limit: 1
          assign own_image = image
        endfor
        capture names
          render 'gs-names', entries: metaobject.artists.value
        endcapture
        assign entry_text = names | strip
        if entry_text != blank
          assign entry_text = entry_text | append: ', '
        endif
        assign entry_text = entry_text | append: metaobject.title.value
        if metaobject.year.value != blank
          assign entry_text = entry_text | append: ', ' | append: metaobject.year.value
        endif
        assign entry_label = entry_text
        if metaobject.medium.value != blank
          assign entry_text = entry_text | append: '. ' | append: metaobject.medium.value
        endif
      when 'artist'
        assign own_image = metaobject.portrait.value
        assign entry_text = metaobject.name.value
        if metaobject.nationality.value != blank
          assign entry_text = entry_text | append: ', ' | append: metaobject.nationality.value
        endif
        if metaobject.life_dates.value != blank
          assign entry_text = entry_text | append: ', ' | append: metaobject.life_dates.value
        endif
        assign bio = metaobject.biography | metafield_text | truncatewords: 30
        if bio != blank
          if entry_text != blank
            assign entry_text = entry_text | append: '. '
          endif
          assign entry_text = entry_text | append: bio
        else
          assign works_note = 'artist'
        endif
      when 'lesson'
        assign own_image = metaobject.cover.value
      when 'collection_group'
        assign entry_text = metaobject.introduction.value | strip_newlines | truncatewords: 30
        if entry_text == blank
          assign works_note = 'group'
        endif
    endcase
  endif
  # Shopify's own description, made from the text with its spaces dropped: it starts as the text
  # does once both have lost their spaces. The page's own words are used instead (DS-160).
  assign stored = page_description
  if stored != blank and made_from != blank
    assign nb = ' '
    assign a = stored | strip_newlines | remove: ' ' | remove: nb | remove: '&amp;' | remove: '&' | slice: 0, 40
    assign b = made_from | strip_html | strip_newlines | remove: ' ' | remove: nb | remove: '&amp;' | remove: '&nbsp;' | remove: '&' | slice: 0, 40
    if a == b
      assign stored = ''
    endif
  endif
  # An edition always describes itself by its label: one form for every edition.
  if request.page_type == 'product' and entry_label != blank
    assign stored = ''
  endif
  if request.page_type == 'index' and settings.home_description != blank
    assign stored = settings.home_description
  endif
  assign description = written | default: stored | default: entry_text
  if works_note != blank and page_description == blank
    # How many works the collection holds. The count comes from the entry looked up by its handle,
    # so the page's own list is still unread when gs-work-grid pages it.
    assign counted = metaobjects[metaobject.system.type][metaobject.system.handle]
    assign works_total = counted.works.value.size | default: 0
    if works_total > 0
      if works_note == 'artist'
        assign note = 'collection.meta.artist_works' | t: count: works_total
        assign description = description | append: '. ' | append: note
      else
        assign description = 'collection.meta.group_works' | t: count: works_total, name: metaobject.name.value
      endif
    endif
  endif
  if description != blank and lead_in != blank
    assign description = lead_in | append: description
  endif
  assign og_description = description
  if og_description == blank and request.page_type == 'index'
    assign og_description = shop.description | default: shop.name
  endif

  if request.page_type == 'product'
    assign og_type = 'product'
  elsif request.page_type == 'article'
    assign og_type = 'article'
  elsif request.page_type == 'password'
    assign og_url = request.origin
  endif

  assign og_image = own_image | default: page_image

  # A grouping's own page number and address (DS-168). The tag's size matches gs-work-grid's.
  assign list_page = current_page
  assign list_prev = ''
  assign list_next = ''
  if metaobject.system.type == 'collection_group'
    paginate metaobject.works.value by 24
      assign list_page = paginate.current_page
      if paginate.previous.is_link
        assign list_prev = paginate.previous.url
        # Page 1 is the grouping's own address, not "page 1" of it.
        if paginate.current_page == 2
          assign list_prev = metaobject.system.url
        endif
      endif
      if paginate.next.is_link
        assign list_next = paginate.next.url
      endif
    endpaginate
  endif
  assign self_url = canonical_url
  if list_page > 1
    # The page's own address: a neighbour's, with this page's number.
    assign neighbour = list_next | default: list_prev
    if neighbour != blank
      assign self_url = neighbour | split: '=' | first | append: '=' | append: list_page | prepend: shop.url
    endif
    assign og_url = self_url
  endif
%}

{%- liquid
  # The name after the bar: the programme whose logo the header shows (DS-121, gs-header).
  capture brand
    render 'gs-brand'
  endcapture
  assign brand = brand | strip
  case brand
    when 'artists-for-kids'
      assign site_name = 'general.site_title.artists_for_kids' | t
    when 'foundation'
      assign site_name = 'general.site_title.foundation' | t
    else
      assign site_name = 'general.site_title.gallery' | t
  endcase
  # A page with no title of its own (the home page by default) shows the programme's name, not the
  # store's (DS-121).
  assign tab_title = page_title | strip
  if entry_label != blank
    assign tab_title = entry_label
  endif
  assign store_name = shop.name | replace: '&amp;', '&'
  if tab_title == store_name or tab_title == shop.name
    assign tab_title = site_name
  endif
  # The link preview's title is the tab's, without the programme's name after the bar.
  if tab_title != blank
    assign og_title = tab_title
  endif
  assign title_key = tab_title | downcase
  assign name_key = site_name | downcase
  assign tags = current_tags | join: ', '
-%}

<meta
  property="og:site_name"
  content="{{ site_name | escape }}"
>
<meta
  property="og:url"
  content="{{ og_url }}"
>
<meta
  property="og:title"
  content="{{ og_title | escape }}"
>
<meta
  property="og:type"
  content="{{ og_type }}"
>
{%- if og_description != blank %}
  <meta
    property="og:description"
    content="{{ og_description | escape }}"
  >
{%- endif %}

{%- if og_image -%}
  <meta
    property="og:image"
    content="https:{{ og_image | image_url: width: 1200 }}"
  >
  <meta
    property="og:image:secure_url"
    content="https:{{ og_image | image_url: width: 1200 }}"
  >
  {%- if og_image.width and og_image.aspect_ratio -%}
    {%- liquid
      assign og_width = og_image.width | at_most: 1200
      assign og_height = og_width | divided_by: og_image.aspect_ratio | round
    -%}
    <meta
      property="og:image:width"
      content="{{ og_width }}"
    >
    <meta
      property="og:image:height"
      content="{{ og_height }}"
    >
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if og_image.alt != blank -%}
    <meta
      property="og:image:alt"
      content="{{ og_image.alt | escape }}"
    >
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}

{%- if request.page_type == 'product' -%}
  <meta
    property="og:price:amount"
    content="{{ product.price | money_without_currency | strip_html }}"
  >
  <meta
    property="og:price:currency"
    content="{{ cart.currency.iso_code }}"
  >
{%- endif -%}

<meta
  name="twitter:card"
  content="summary_large_image"
>
{%- if og_image %}
  <meta
    name="twitter:image"
    content="https:{{ og_image | image_url: width: 1200 }}"
  >
  {%- if og_image.alt != blank %}
    <meta
      name="twitter:image:alt"
      content="{{ og_image.alt | escape }}"
    >
  {%- endif %}
{%- endif %}
<meta
  name="twitter:title"
  content="{{ og_title | escape }}"
>
{%- if og_description != blank %}
  <meta
    name="twitter:description"
    content="{{ og_description | escape }}"
  >
{%- endif %}

<title>
  {%- case template.name -%}
    {%- when 'cart' -%}
      {{- 'cart.title' | t -}}
    {%- when '404' -%}
      {{- 'not_found.title' | t -}}
    {%- when 'search' -%}
      {%- if search.performed -%}
        {%- comment -%} The same count as the page's summary: Shopify's results and the entries (DS-113). {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- assign search_count = search.results_count -%}
        {%- assign entry_kinds = 'exhibition,lesson,artist' | split: ',' -%}
        {%- for kind in entry_kinds -%}
          {%- capture ids -%}{%- render 'gs-search-entries', kind: kind, terms: search.terms -%}{%- endcapture -%}
          {%- assign ids = ids | strip | split: ',' -%}
          {%- assign search_count = search_count | plus: ids.size -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
        {{- 'search.results' | t: count: search_count, terms: search.terms -}}
      {%- else -%}
        {{- 'search.title' | t -}}
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- else -%}
      {{- tab_title | escape_once -}}
  {%- endcase -%}
  {%- if current_tags %}, {{ 'general.title_tagged' | t: tags: tags }}{% endif -%}
  {%- if list_page != 1 %}, {{ 'general.title_page' | t: number: list_page }}{% endif -%}
  {%- unless title_key contains name_key %} | {{ site_name }}{% endunless -%}
</title>

<link
  rel="canonical"
  href="{{ self_url }}"
>
{%- if list_prev != blank %}
  <link
    rel="prev"
    href="{{ list_prev | prepend: shop.url }}"
  >
{%- endif %}
{%- if list_next != blank %}
  <link
    rel="next"
    href="{{ list_next | prepend: shop.url }}"
  >
{%- endif %}

{%- comment -%} A frame is sold only with its print (DS-137), so its own page stays out of search engines. {%- endcomment -%}
{% if template.name == 'product' and product.type == 'Frame' %}
  <meta name="robots" content="noindex">
{% else %}
  <meta name="robots" content="max-image-preview:large, max-snippet:-1, max-video-preview:-1">
{% endif %}

{% if description != blank %}
  <meta
    name="description"
    content="{{ description | escape }}"
  >
{% endif %}

{% render 'gs-data', description: description, label: entry_label, image: og_image %}
